## Module 9 delivered (do not regress)

- Retrieval modes: `embedding_only`, `hybrid_static`, `hybrid_with_history`
- Embedding-only baseline remains independently executable
- Deterministic diagnostic signal extraction and hybrid query builder (masked/bounded)
- Enriched knowledge chunk metadata; lexical exact-match index
- Versioned weight profiles (`embedding_baseline_v1`, `hybrid_static_v1`, `hybrid_history_v1`)
- Hybrid scorer with active-weight normalisation; deterministic rerank/dedupe/diversity
- Organisation-scoped historical incident index (no migration; citations via JSON metadata)
- `ENABLE_HISTORICAL_RETRIEVAL=false` by default; clients cannot bypass server flags
- Module 8 retrieval-quality and post-retrieval routing consume hybrid results
- Soft-fail retrieval; weak retrieval still blocks unsupported external reasoning

## Module 8 delivered (do not regress)

- Two-stage adaptive routing (`AdaptiveExecutionRouter`): initial (pre-retrieval) and post-retrieval
- Typed Module 8 models: modes, routes, confidence/evidence/uncertainty/retrieval assessments, budget, fusion
- Heuristic `RuleBasedConfidenceCalibrator` (not statistical probability)
- Evidence-quality, uncertainty, and retrieval-quality evaluators (deterministic, no LLM)
- `AIExecutionBudgetManager` with Decimal costs; unknown pricing stays null; local = not_applicable
- Latency stage tracking with budget checks before expensive stages
- Controlled `DiagnosisFusionService` and `FinalConfidenceRecalibrator`
- Provider interfaces for embeddings, vector store, and reasoning (Module 7)
- Soft-fail RAG/LLM stages with deterministic classifier/template fallback
- Persist routing, confidence, cost, latency and evaluation metadata in existing JSON fields
- `ENABLE_RAG` / `ENABLE_LLM` remain off by default; request options cannot bypass server flags
- Baseline modes preserved: `rules_only`, `rules_rag`, `llm_only`, `rag_llm`, `confidence_routed`
- Versioned policy `confidence_cost_policy` / `v1` with stable configuration hash

## Step 3–4 infrastructure (do not regress)

- Persistent Chroma Docker service (`chromadb/chroma:1.5.9`, volume `chroma_data`)
- Real local embeddings: `EMBEDDING_PROVIDER=sentence_transformers` + `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` (CPU default)
- Hash embeddings remain the deterministic default; never silently fall back ST → hash
- Model cache volume `model_cache`; CLI `app.cli.warmup_embeddings` / `app.cli.test_embeddings`
- See `docs/EMBEDDING_SETUP.md`

